  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Little change to the forecast reasoning and\nsynoptic setups through Thu. Where guidance is fairly well \nclustered is with an amplified upper trough that will be \nshifting east out of the Central U.S. A progressive and open \nwave will sweep through the Eastern U.S at the end of the week. \nBefore that happens, low level flow will switch to southeast \ntoday as weak warm front/coastal trough lifts through, which \nwill produce some widely sct showers. The increased moisture \nwill also support patchy, dense fog inland of the coast this \nmorning, and likely again tonight. Continued higher than \nadvertised NBM pops for these widely scattered showers, best \nchances during diurnal heating. No real accums of rain expected,\nbut enough to wet the ground in places. Area is firmly \nentrenched in swrly flow Thu, but with no forcing in place, pops\nare generally less than 15% except for the OBX, which may ocnl \nbe plagued by some showers skirting the coast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Friday - Still looks like widespread showers \nand even a few thunderstorms (during the afternoon) into \nevening with a wet cold front moving through. Of note, some \nguidance shows anomalous moisture and higher- than- normal \ninstability for early November, as indicated by EFI highlighting\nCAPE vals nearing the 80th percentile. Have increased the \nthunder threat for inland areas where the EFI is highlighting \nthe higher CAPE/Shear indices, with slght chc thunder probs for \ncoastal counties. If best forcing lines up with peak heating, a \nstrong to severe thunderstorm threat would materialize for areas\nesp west of Hwy 17 Fri afternoon. Main threat would be damaging\nwinds. \n\nVery warm and humid airmass in place, and nighttime lows will \nesp be very warm, and be closer to our normal highs for this \ntime of year. Some record warm lows may be in jeopardy. Highs\nthrough Fri will be near 80 inland with 70s coast, and lows will\nbe in the 60s. For reference, normal highs are 65-70 for early \nNovember, with normal lows in the 40s inland and 50s along the \ncoast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Good agreement amongst models with fropa late\nFri, which will usher in a more seasonably dry airmass for the \ncoming weekend. Return to mo sunny skies and highs in the upper\n60s to low 70s, and lows generally in the 40s. Warmest day will\nbe Sat.",
